cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EDEA-EOKit in your work, please cite this software and the associated paper."
title: "EDEA-EOKit: a tested and reproducible Python chain for surface water and flood mapping from optical satellite imagery"
version: 1.0.3
date-released: 2026-11-21
type: software
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  EDEA-EOKit reads a multiband GeoTIFF, applies the correct radiometric scaling for the
  sensor, masks clouds, computes NDWI, MNDWI, AWEI and NDVI, converts pixels into hectares
  using the real ground size of a pixel, and quantifies the optimistic bias of random
  validation designs against spatial block cross-validation.
